"The Howard train is a run of long steel cars with plastic seats, bright lights and heat blowing low."
"The doors chime and slide shut some fifteen seconds after they open."
"A recorded voice names each stop: Addison, Sheridan, Wilson, and on north to Howard."
"Howard is the end of the line, some twenty-five minutes north; every rider must get off there."
"No one checks fares aboard; a rider already past the turnstiles rides free."
"At five on a Saturday morning a car holds a few riders: a man asleep, a nurse in scrubs, a student."
"A screen by the doors runs ads and news: the hero Skiff chased an earth-shaper under Lake Michigan."
"The heat in the car makes numb feet burn and prickle as feeling comes back."
"Riders glance at a barefoot woman in a sleep shirt and mostly look away."
"The nurse is kind but tired, and would ask a shoeless woman if she needs help."
